  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "One server-side gate",
      "items": [
        "visibleEntries = authz.VisibleResourceIDs union Entry.IsPublic; a restricted record without a grant stays invisible even when approved.",
        "registry.Discoverable(entries) then keeps only approved resources; an empty status is treated as approved for legacy rows.",
        "GET /api/resources?discoverable=true, GET /api/workspace, MCP / Agent Card export and A2A selection all reuse this gate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What the desktop client does",
      "items": [
        "ThreadView and PersonaEditor call listResources('agent', { discoverable: true }) and render the response as-is.",
        "No client-side status filter: a second curation gate would let the desktop override the server's approval.",
        "A failed @mention is reported by reason code (not_found / not_approved / forbidden / delegate_failed) in 13 locales.",
        "OrgView uses the unflagged listResources() for curation; it still passes the same visibility filter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who can change a grant",
      "items": [
        "Curators use GET/POST /api/grants and DELETE /api/grants/{id} (grants:manage); status changes use POST /api/resources/{id}/status (registry:curate).",
        "Grants live in PostgreSQL resource_grants; creating a resource auto-grants its creator LevelWrite.",
        "agentbuddy has no grants UI or API wrapper: the loopback proxy only forwards /api, /a2a, /healthz and /.well-known.",
        "Thread @mention resolution reuses resolvableEntries = Discoverable and canAccess, then delegates via Hub.Send directly."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
